Subject: [PATCH] latex: let a document read figures and other non-tex inputs

A paper is more than its .tex files. The srcs of latex_document
accepted .tex alone, so a figure could not be named as a dependency
and \includegraphics had nothing to find. The rule already copies
every src into the work directory under its package relative path, so
accepting the other file types a document reads is the whole change.

Upstream as https://github.com/filmil/bazel_rules_latex_host/pull/5;
drop this patch when a release carries it.

diff --git a/latex/defs.bzl b/latex/defs.bzl
index 99a0bf2..ca75e1a 100644
--- a/latex/defs.bzl
+++ b/latex/defs.bzl
@@ -59,7 +59,31 @@ _latex_document = rule(
     implementation = _latex_document_impl,
     attrs = {
         "main": attr.string(mandatory = True, doc = "Main .tex filename in this package."),
-        "srcs": attr.label_list(allow_files = [".tex"], mandatory = True),
+        # A document is more than its .tex files: figures, a bibliography,
+        # and a class or style file that ships with the paper rather than
+        # with the TeX distribution. Every one of them is copied into the
+        # work directory under its package relative path, so
+        # \includegraphics{figures/plot} finds figures/plot.png.
+        "srcs": attr.label_list(
+            allow_files = [
+                ".tex",
+                ".sty",
+                ".cls",
+                ".clo",
+                ".bib",
+                ".bst",
+                ".png",
+                ".jpg",
+                ".jpeg",
+                ".pdf",
+                ".eps",
+                ".ps",
+                ".svg",
+                ".csv",
+                ".dat",
+            ],
+            mandatory = True,
+        ),
     },
     toolchains = [_TC],
 )
@@ -70,7 +94,10 @@ def latex_document(name, main, deps = [], visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
     Args:
       name: target name.
       main: the main .tex file (e.g. "paper.tex").
-      deps: extra inputs it `\\input`s (e.g. glob(["sections/*.tex"])).
+      deps: extra inputs the document reads: files it `\\input`s, and the
+        figures, bibliography, class or style files it names (e.g.
+        glob(["sections/*.tex"]) + glob(["figures/*.png"])). Each is
+        copied into the work directory under its package relative path.
       visibility: target visibility (public by default so a `combined_pdf`
         target can consume the produced PDF across packages).
       **kwargs: forwarded to the underlying rule.
